      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19739",
      ":question/problem": "Use a midpoint Riemann sum with the partition\n$[- 2, 3] = [- 2, 0]\u222a[0, 1]\u222a[1, 2]\u222a[2, 3]$\nto approximate the area under the curve of the continuous function $y = f(x)$ whose data is given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ | $2.5$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $1.25$ | $2$ | $3.25$ | $5$ | $7.25$ | $10$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
